I have read alis, and wouldn't use {la} any different.

One thing that stood out for me in oz is the use of {la} to refer to
bunches of individuals, such as {la maxpre} being used to refer to
Munchkins in general, as well as to the Munchkins Dorothy first finds after
landing in Oz. Similarly for {la .kalid=C4=81s.}.

I agree with Pierre that {la maxpre} should never be "the Munchkin" or
"some Munchkins", but instead "Munchkin", unless
it is a common name shared by all these folks, like "Joe Munchkin", "Paul
Munchkin", "Mary Munchkin", etc.

mu'o
mi'e .asiz.

